```text
6. Fix file-block and deletelist parsing in apply_file_changes
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Replace brittle literal-newline regexes with permissive delimiters-bounded patterns (matching the proven external script approach)
        - Replace file_blocks regex with: re.compile(r'¤\s*filepath\s*=\s*(["\'])(.*?)\1\s*¤\s*(.*?)\s*¤\s*filepath\s*=\s*\1\2\1\s*¤', re.DOTALL); iterate with finditer; group(2)=path, group(3)=raw_content
        - Replace deletelist parsing: if "¤deletelist¤" in raw_text, split on that sentinel, then finditer a permissive pattern r'¤\s*filepath\s*=\s*(["\'])(.*?)\1\s*¤' over the remainder; collect group(2)
        - Add .strip() to each extracted path before calling _prefix_path (the proven script strips at write time)
        - Add .strip("\n") to cleaned content before passing to self.files.write_file (strips residual leading/trailing newlines from regex capture)
        - Prohibition: do not change _prefix_path, write_file, delete_file, or IngestApplyResult — only the parsing and content-cleaning layer changes
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Replace _clean_content with first/last-fence-index slicing
        - New implementation: splitlines(); scan forward for first line whose .strip().startswith("```"), set start_idx = i+1; scan backward for last such line, set end_idx = i; if start_idx < end_idx, slice lines[start_idx:end_idx]; return "\n".join(lines)
        - This handles fences that are not the absolute first/last lines (e.g. blank lines or prose before the opening fence), and handles \r\n via splitlines()
        - Prohibition: do not change the @staticmethod decorator or the method signature
```
```text
1. Sidepanel mode buttons: add Enter key handler
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/sidepanel-left.js': Add keydown listener to mode buttons so Enter activates them
        - In onConnect(), alongside the existing click listener, attach a keydown listener to each [data-mode] button
        - If event.key === 'Enter': call event.stopPropagation() then event.preventDefault(), then invoke this.#switchMode(button.dataset.mode)
        - This mirrors the kb-bar pattern: stopPropagation prevents the document-level handler in clanker-app.js from intercepting Enter and calling preventDefault, which would suppress the native button activation
```
